---
const canonicalUrl = 'https://alat.cc/products/ujer/privacy-policy/'
const contactEmail = 'azzam@alat.cc'
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <meta name="description" content="Privacy Policy for Ujer." />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="alat" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Ujer Privacy Policy — alat" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Privacy Policy for Ujer." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl} />
    <title>Ujer Privacy Policy — alat</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header shell">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="alat home">alat<span>.</span></a>
      <a class="back-link" href="/products/ujer/">← Ujer</a>
    </header>

    <main class="shell policy-page">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Ujer</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: November 9, 2026</p>

      <p class="lead">
        Ujer is a dictation app for Android and macOS. This policy explains
        what information Ujer handles when you use it.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Microphone and keyboard</h2>
        <p>Ujer accesses the microphone after you grant permission and start recording.
          The Android keyboard sends text you type or dictate to the app and text field
          you are using. Dictation is disabled in password and private fields.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Audio and transcription</h2>
        <p>Ujer records audio on your device and sends it for transcription when you
          stop recording. With your own API key, audio is sent to the provider and
          endpoint you configure. That provider's terms and privacy policy govern
          its processing and retention.</p>
        <p>With Ujer Pro, audio is sent to Alat Auth and an AI service provider for
          transcription. If you enable the optional cleanup feature, the transcript
          is also sent for AI processing. Your selected language and personal
          dictionary terms may be sent as transcription hints. Service providers
          process this information to provide the requested feature.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Account, settings and usage</h2>
        <p>Ujer Pro uses Google sign-in and an Alat Auth account. We receive account
          information such as your email address and Google account identifier to
          authenticate you. Account, session, credit and usage records support
          access, billing, security and service operation.</p>
        <p>If you use your own API key, Ujer stores your provider settings and key
          on your device and sends the key to your configured provider to authorize
          requests. Android uses Keystore-backed storage for secrets; macOS uses
          Keychain. The provider and model you choose determine where your audio goes.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Local data and retention</h2>
        <p>On Android, Ujer can keep transcripts and unsuccessful or unconfirmed
          recordings on your device. Successful recordings are removed from local
          app storage; saved results and failed recordings remain until you delete
          them. On macOS, recordings and related metadata can be stored locally;
          files at least seven days old are removed when the recording store is
          next maintained. Text inserted into another app or copied to the clipboard
          is subject to that app's or operating system's handling.</p>
        <p>Account and usage records are retained for operating the service and
          managing credits. AI providers may retain information under their own
          policies. Contact us for details about retention or deletion of your data.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="account-deletion">
        <h2>Request account and data deletion</h2>
        <p>To request deletion of your Ujer Pro account and associated data, email
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}?subject=Ujer%20account%20deletion%20request`}>{contactEmail}</a>
          from the address associated with your account. We may need to verify your
          identity before processing the request. You can also delete locally saved
          results in Ujer or clear the app's data. For data held by a provider you
          configured with your own API key, contact that provider directly.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or requests, contact
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="shell footer-note">
      <p>Useful software, quietly made.</p>
      <span>alat.cc / 2026</span>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap');
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(body) { background: #151613; color: #f1efe7; font-family: 'Manrope', sans-serif; margin: 0; }
  :global(a) { color: inherit; }
  :global(code) { color: #d7f96a; font: 0.9em 'DM Mono', monospace; }
  .shell { margin: 0 auto; width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 48px)); }
  .site-header { align-items: center; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 30px 0; }
  .wordmark { font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.08em; text-decoration: none; }
  .wordmark span, .eyebrow span { color: #d7f96a; }
  .back-link, .eyebrow, .updated, .footer-note span { color: #85867c; font: 0.68rem 'DM Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .back-link { text-decoration: none; }
  .back-link:hover, a:hover { color: #d7f96a; }
  .policy-page { max-width: 760px; padding: 72px 0 120px; }
  .eyebrow { color: #d7f96a; }
  .eyebrow span { display: inline-block; margin-right: 9px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 7rem); letter-spacing: -0.1em; line-height: 0.9; margin: 28px 0 18px; }
  .updated { margin: 0; }
  .lead { color: #f1efe7; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 64px 0 0; }
  section { border-top: 1px solid #373832; margin-top: 54px; padding-top: 18px; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.05em; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  p { color: #aaa9a0; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  section a { color: #d7f96a; }
  .footer-note { align-items: end; border-top: 1px solid #373832; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 22px 0 34px; }
  .footer-note p { color: #85867c; font-size: 0.78rem; margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .shell { width: min(100% - 32px, 1120px); }
    .policy-page { padding-top: 72px; }
    .lead { margin-top: 48px; }
    .footer-note { align-items: start; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
  }
</style>
